# L §5.10 Sign rules, E §4.2 step 5 (tally 2.1.8 R11): "A balance that breaks the rule at one of these points is
# refused from there to the place's next reading", whether a leg, a reading's pad or an anchor broke it. jar (min 0) is
# stated -50.00 PLN on 2026-03-20 with a pad: refused from there (a), the pad's own reading doesn't end it; the next
# reading, 70.00 PLN on 2026-04-20, does (b). jar2 is the anchor twin. 2.1.7's refcore kept both refused after the
# second reading (T's c2).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place jar: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place jar2: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[jar] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[jar2] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  pad jar from world
  anchor jar2
  stated[jar] = -50.00 PLN at 2026-03-20 end "s"
  stated[jar2] = -50.00 PLN at 2026-03-20 end "s"

version st2
  cite s
  governs 2026-04
  known 2026-05-02
  pad jar from world
  anchor jar2
  stated[jar] = 70.00 PLN at 2026-04-20 end "s"
  stated[jar2] = 70.00 PLN at 2026-04-20 end "s"

ask a: bal(jar, 2026-03-21), bal(jar2, 2026-03-21)
ask b: bal(jar, 2026-04-21), bal(jar2, 2026-04-21)
=== expect
a: (refused: RUN-PLACE pads:st:jar@2026-03-20 end takes jar below 0, refused: RUN-PLACE jar2 is -50.00 PLN after its reading at 2026-03-20 end)
  anchor: jar2 2026-03-20 end, stated -50.00 PLN, difference -150.00 PLN
  pad: jar 2026-03-20 end, pads:st:jar@2026-03-20 end of -150.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-10
b: (70.00 PLN, 70.00 PLN)
  anchor: jar2 2026-04-20 end, stated 70.00 PLN, difference refused: RUN-PLACE jar2 is -50.00 PLN after its reading at 2026-03-20 end
  pad: jar 2026-04-20 end, pads:st2:jar@2026-04-20 end of refused: RUN-PLACE pads:st:jar@2026-03-20 end takes jar below 0
  cut 2026-06-10
